{"kind":"report","text":"Exact MCP review: 3e3d016f6f2166be2b5a6089d01261b558faf301, tree da27b41743c357016991f9a6dc00b68bcfd05900. Changes requested: one additional P2.\n\nP2 — a valid local fact selector loses its expected revision. shape.ts shapes a declared fact as its original FactRef; effectiveFields applies defaults but leaves that object intact. expectedOf, lines132–156, resolves also.by only when the field is numeric. service.ts409 feeds this view into expectedOf and signs the incomplete expected map. Native derive/fields.ts172–211 verifies a local fact and converts it to seq before handlers.alsoItems selects the item; judge requires that alias's expected revision. An otherwise valid generic action is therefore refused bad-intent.\n\nConcrete static case: a pantry-like act declares jarFact:{type:fact,under:pantry,kind:[fill],required:true} and selected:{item:jar,by:jarFact}. Its caller provides the exact local fill receipt for an existing jar, distinct from the primary shelf. Native definition validation permits this selector; the local receipt's seq names the opened jar. MCP advertises FactRef input but signs no selected revision. This is supplied-input normalization, not an assertion that a default local fact is possible, an executed counterexample, or an authority bypass.\n\nResolve subjects with the native effective values, including declared local-fact normalization using the target scope/incarnation, while retaining the original signed FactRef and requested-meaning digest. Do not turn a foreign fact's seq into a local item ID or weaken native fact validation. Add a real Worker generic witness for valid local-fact selection, original signed field preservation, the alias revision, and revision-moved after the selected item changes.\n\nArchitecture: the prior item-default P2 is repaired. The temporary default view and act/join integration preserve sparse signed input, explicit overrides and no-default omission; the new native test checks accepted omission, alias revision, explicit second jar, a retained prepared envelope refused after shake, and no-default absence. Prepared here is the kept-envelope phase; the fixture does not prove an accepted native hold stage. The new finding shows why generic subject preparation must follow both native defaulting and local-fact normalization. Existing holds, replay, discovery and two-file publication retain qualified Source authority. Full Stage 2, CLI-guide and credential-read duties remain owed; f9 app discovery stays separate after this build lands.\n\nSecurity: own-property reads and safe writes continue to preserve lawful prototype names. Native revision/fact checks correctly refuse an incomplete or invalid intent; no privilege bypass is claimed. Custody, key/session/transport guards and bounded errors are unchanged. No private credential, log, recipe, generated body or provider/browser action was performed by checker.\n\nSimplification: the default helper is narrow and does not mutate the signed input. Preserve that distinction while aligning expected-subject resolution with native semantics. Service CallResult bounds, the separately measured modern 110-byte metadata, marked-minimum fallback and lease-interval witness retain prior qualified coverage.\n\nEvidence: primary FIRST logical FULL: 45,123 bytes / 482 LF SHA 7b57edf153030cfcb28eef6306ee4626437da7eb952e42d9b98460e2466ba934, native prior 50 ranges plus all 3,713 fresh bytes before other Source. All 60 artifacts bound; 54 whole bodies equal 50 and six fresh paths. Peer finals/audits and Root native checks qualify fresh bodies/U3 and inherited content. Tools JSON remains lossless-token FULL rather than raw-body FULL; lock and indices retain partial credit. All 1,422 unrelated current-main b69 paths are preserved.\n\nThe exact admitted public gate projection was FULL, 2,511 bytes, Root-measured SHA 404dfbe7808ae4538863a23e7ac12933e1604424f3d84f6ac7a84aa71a4754b6. Invitation supplied the SHA of SHA256SUMS, not the body;